    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Downloaded .exe in user Downloads carries Mark-of-the-Web (Zone.Identifier ADS)", "technique": "T1553.005", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-17 14:42:10 UTC, Sysmon EID 11 captured creation of C:\\Users\\r.santaolalla\\Downloads\\p120_144210\\corp_update.exe by powershell.exe; AMSI 4104 then shows operator reading Zone.Identifier ADS containing 'ZoneId=3' AND 'HostUrl=https://attacker.example/payload.exe'. Rule 92002 triggered.", "chain_reason": "MOTW with ZoneId=3 (Internet) is the OS-level signal that a file came from an untrusted source. Phishing droppers must strip this to avoid SmartScreen prompts."},
